_silica_rt_build_int_range_list:        ; @silica_rt_build_int_range_list
	.cfi_startproc
; X0 = start, X1 = count -> X0 = the List[int64, mem(normal)] [start .. start + count - 1], or 0
; (nil) when count <= 0 or the region is exhausted. The layout is the one the compiled list prims
; read (prims_list.silica): a 24-byte handle {length, first chunk, cursor} over 32-byte chunks
; {two int64 slots filled back to front, next chunk at +16, claim at +24}. The elements go in
; from the last to the first, so every chunk after the first is full (cursor 0) as
; L_list_tail_helper expects when it steps to a successor, and the first chunk's claim equals its
; cursor so a later prepend takes its free slot in place. Allocation is the actor's region, as
; the compiled prepend allocates, so the list is released with the actor that asked for it.
; Earlier this built 16-byte cons cells {value, next}: read as a handle, the first value was the
; length and the next cell the chunk, which is what cpu_topology_runtime_queries faulted on.
